{
  "_comment": [
    "One table, two implementations. jarvis-core's `parse_reference` +",
    "`permits` in skills/install.py decide whether a skill may be fetched;",
    "the console copies the rule into `whyNotReference` so the install form",
    "can refuse a pasted URL without a round trip. A copy that drifts is",
    "worse than no copy, because the form would accept what the server then",
    "rejects and the reader would blame the form. Both suites read THIS",
    "file, so drift breaks whichever side moved.",
    "`ok` is 'the server would fetch this'. Everything else \u2014 malformed,",
    "off the allow-list, a URL \u2014 is one refusal as far as the form is",
    "concerned, because the form's job is to stop the press, not to grade",
    "the mistake."
  ],
